    // MARK: - query — a CONCRETE default, at the layer TypeScript puts it

    /// Run a GraphQL document against this MFE's BFF.
    ///
    /// `BaseMFE.doQuery` is the one hook that is NOT abstract: it is a working
    /// default on the base class (ADR-053, ADR-070), so this is rendered here
    /// rather than on a subclass. An MFE with no BFF and no override answers
    /// `data: nil` instead of dialing a non-existent endpoint, which is what
    /// makes the capability uniform across every MFE (ADR-070).
    ///
    /// Endpoint resolution, in the order ADR-053 fixes:
    ///   1. `context.inputs["bffUrl"]`
    ///   2. the `BFF_URL` environment variable
    ///   3. `identity.bffEndpoint` — the manifest's, baked at generation
    ///
